{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>To fear Me and to keep, etc.</b> The reason He did not subsume the category of guarding under the general statement of fear — perhaps it is because from the side of fear one bad particular emerged, for this was the cause that Israel made the calf: when they saw that Moses delayed, fear and dread fell upon them, since there was no Moses to be the emissary to speak with them, HaShem would again speak with them as at first. Therefore they rushed to make the calf, thinking it would serve as an intermediary and speak to them the words of HaShem. And you will find that they of blessed memory said (Tanchuma, Ki Tissa) that the calf actually spoke, and they erred in it as an intermediary. Therefore HaShem was precise in His statement and said <b>to fear Me and to keep My commandments</b> — that the fear should be for them also to keep, and they would not stray from the side of those who fear HaShem." "<b>That it may be well, etc.</b> Meaning: His saying ״מִי יִתֵּן״ etc. was not for the benefit of saying it, but out of love of the good to be said of Him."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:15:30.681786132Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}